<title>GERMANY: German call money markets closed for holiday.</title>
<headline>German call money markets closed for holiday.</headline>
<dateline>FRANKFURT 1996-10-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>German call money markets were closed on Thursday for a national German holiday. Regular trading resumes on Friday.</p>
<p>Call money rates on Wednesday eased to 3.025/3.075 percent from Tuesday's 3.05/3.15 percent as the money market continued to recover from its month-end strains that pushed rates as high as 4.50 percent on Monday.</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom +49 69 756525</p>
